<name>Starting</name>
<ttl id="10024_S000T_744HN_T007Z" variety="T007Z">
<name>Smart Entry &amp; Start System (Start System)</name>
<para id="X39400000IL00JJ" category="J" type-id="30531" name-id="161XL-00" from="200612">
<dtccode/>
<dtcname>Engine does not start</dtcname>
<subpara id="X39400000IL00JJ_10" type-id="31" category="03" proc-id="RM0550J___00004B500000">
<name>Circuit Description</name>
<content5 releasenbr="1">
<list1 type="nonmark">
<item>
<ptxt>When the electrical key transmitter (electronic key) is in the cabin, pressing the engine switch causes the instrument panel J/B assembly (main body ECU) to receive a signal and switch the power source mode. In addition, pushing the engine switch while depressing the brake pedal with the shift position in P or N starts the engine.</ptxt>
</item>
</list1>
<atten3>
<list1 type="unordered">
<item>
<ptxt>When using the TaSCAN with the IG OFF, repeatedly turn any door courtesy light switch ON and OFF (at intervals of 1.5 seconds or less) until communication between the TaSCAN and the vehicle starts.</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>The Smart Entry &amp; Start System (start system) has functions that use multiplex communication. First, follow "How to Proceed with Troubleshooting" and confirm that there is no malfunction in the communication system before proceeding with troubleshooting.</ptxt>
</item>
</list1>
</atten3>
<atten4>
<ptxt>When the instrument panel J/B assembly (main body ECU) is replaced with a new ECU and the battery negative terminal is connected, it enters the IG ON state. Also, when the battery is removed and reinstalled, it returns to the state it was in when the battery was removed.</ptxt>
</atten4>
</content5>
</subpara>
<subpara id="X39400000IL00JJ_11" type-id="32" category="03" proc-id="RM0550J___00004B600000">
<name>Wiring Diagram</name>
<content5 releasenbr="1">
<figure>
<graphic graphicname="A161613J01" width="7.106578999in" height="8.799559038in"/>
</figure>
</content5>
</subpara>
<subpara id="X39400000IL00JJ_12" type-id="51" category="05" proc-id="RM0550J___00004B700000">
<name>Inspection Procedure</name>
<content5 releasenbr="1">
<atten4>
<ptxt>When the smart key computer assembly (certification ECU), immobiliser code computer (ID code box) or steering lock actuator (steering lock ECU) has been replaced, refer to the immobiliser registration procedure in the reference section.</ptxt>
</atten4>
</content5>
</subpara>
<subpara id="X39400000IL00JJ_18" type-id="01" category="01">
<name>Procedure</name>
<testgrp id="X39400000IL00JJ_18_0035" proc-id="RM0550J___00004B800000">
<testtitle>Inspect Engine Start (Steering Lock Initialization)</testtitle>
<content6 releasenbr="1">
<test1>
<ptxt>Move the shift lever to the P position.</ptxt>
</test1>
<test1>
<ptxt>With the IG OFF, open and close the driver side door, then check whether the engine starts.</ptxt>
<spec>
<title>Specified Condition</title>
<specitem>
<ptxt>Engine starts</ptxt>
</specitem>
</spec>
<atten4>
<ptxt>After the battery has been discharged, the engine may not start unless the steering lock actuator (steering lock ECU) is initialized using the above procedure.</ptxt>
</atten4>
</test1>
</content6>
<res>
<down ref="X39400000IL00JJ_18_0076" fin="true">OK</down>
<right ref="X39400000IL00JJ_18_0036" fin="false">NG</right>
</res>
</testgrp>
